   "description": "Lachlan Neville is a musician and songwriter from Rocanville, Saskatchewan, whose early passion for reading introduced him to the worlds of Tolkien, C.S. Lewis, and Steinbeck before he left elementary school. This love of literature, paired with the influence of his father\u2019s \u201962 Martin acoustic guitar, guided Lachlan toward the work of Bob Dylan, Townes Van Zandt, Guy Clark, and John Prine, inspiring a deep commitment to songwriting. During the global pandemic, he dedicated time to refining his craft, developing a body of original material that quickly earned recognition.\n\nDoors are at 8pm, show time is 10pm.",
